  "data": {
    "body": "Suppose that $A$ and $B$ are $3 \\times 3$ matrices with $\\operatorname{det}(A)=3$, $\\operatorname{det}(B)=1$. Which of the following statement(s) is/are always TRUE?\n\n\n\n(I) The matrix product $A B$ is invertible.\n\n(II) $\\operatorname{det}(2 A)=6$.\n\n(III) $\\operatorname{det}\\left(A^{-1} B\\right)=\\frac{1}{3}$.",
